<description>&lt;p&gt;President Paul Biya has finally announced a date for the long-delayed national elections, ending his prolonged absence from public view. The African Bar Association has called for mediation in the Anglophone crisis while the UN Human Rights Committee released findings on Cameroon’s situation. Nigeria, Cameroon, Chad and Niger have approved a 5 km cross-border military pursuit to combat terrorism, extending security operations beyond national borders. Ex-rebel fighters remain caught between hiding and broken promises, and activist Agbor Balla warned that a decade of bloodshed still prevents children from safely returning to school in the conflict zones. The conflict recorded 231 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE4yak00RWUyNDRjRlg1UWlCeklTTmp1a2tLVHE5M3lxbE1tRnA5MGtCUnJPTlV1cjBPSVRLSHpUaEl2NU50NzlFUEZxc0RxUDlFR1NyTnB6aXRKbTdGamJBYWpKRGw2UmRQcjJZdTUtZDdqQ0h4S3BSeFg3ZHZ6UQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;dailystruggle.ng&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxOU1VldndZSXBMYnFjZzc1Z3hyREE3bUljdG9nN2t1d3JNMVpIZlhwVXlGTFNpa09WMXM0TkJFTkstNmV0YVRWUmN2SF9Nd19ZOE5iazhBNi1SZ3QwRHJQUS0zWGVqeUgyeHhuVXNHUEtWQmhybVppbE91WGFjZjVFWm5YVjI?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Express Newspaper Mareeba, Atherton, Cooktown, Kuranda&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxOd1phb0wyRTdKTENzVGx0Mjd1d0NVeWtfeTNsNTJxS2JGd2NJMWVsdkM2N1hxc0ZyclBHWE8zYUx1WURMSFdaMzBrRFZTUWQ1Ml9STGJMY25GNHM3YmdUU2FLWlg2Zjc3YTAwa0Z3cjRyV0RfUl9Xb3hZTlBWQ210NzZZOFQ1Zw?oc=5&quot;&gt;dailystruggle.ng&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxPNE04Z0dyU3